Viewer: the resolution follows the window; one switch picks custom or automatic (2026-10-23).

Automatic forced every window shape up to 1280 on the long side. A 2/3 window was therefore 1280x848 (three
rows) until the full screen (1372x686) was used for the first time; then the whole set was scaled to 1372,
the 2/3 area shrank to 876x580 (two rows), and returning to it looked like a resolution change even though
the window had not changed. Automatic now keeps each window's true size (only the 480 short-side floor and
the 1920/2560 cap), so the same 2/3 window stays 876x580 whether or not the full screen has been used.
The display settings have one switch, custom resolution (off: follow the window), instead of an automatic
switch plus width/height fields; the UI size (icon count) stays. Tests: a small page keeps its size, and a
2/3 window does not shrink when the full shape joins.

